ion)  | \nSmall Claims  | Order  | Order for Release of Funds  | \nSmall Claims  | Order  | ORDER OF DISMISSAL PURSUANT TO 1167.1 CCP  | \nSmall Claims  | Order  | Order on Application to Stay Levy or Garnishment (Wage Garnishment - Enforcement of Judgment) (WG-018/EJ-138)  | \nSmall Claims  | Order  | Order on Media Request to Permit Coverage  | \nSmall Claims  | Order  | Order on Request to Correct or Cancel Judgment  | \nSmall Claims  | Order  | Order Regarding Remote Appearance  | \nSmall Claims  | Order  | Order to Set Aside / Vacate (name extension)  | \nSmall Claims  | Party  | Association of Attorney  | \nSmall Claims  | Party  | Authorization to Appear on Behalf of Party (Small Claims)  | \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPP-015/FW-015-INFO (https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/app015info.pdf)\nciteturn2146search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.1 years ago; APP-015/FW-015-INFO\nYou may be ordered to go to court to answer questions about \nyour ability to pay court fees and costs and to provide proof of eligibility. Any initial fee waiver you are granted may \nbe ended if you do not go to court when asked. You may be ordered to repay amounts that were waived if the court \nfinds you were not eligible for the fee waiver.  \n• \nIf you receive a fee waiver, you must tell the court if there is a change in your finances. You must tell  the court \nimmediately if your finances improve or if you become able to pay court fees or costs during this case (file form \nFW-010 with the court). You may be ordered to repay any amounts that were waived after your eligibility ended. If the \ntrial court waived your fees and costs and you settle your case for $10,000 or more, the trial court will have a lien on \nthe settlement in the amount of the waived fees. \nThe fee waiver ends. The fee waiver expires 60 days after the judgment, dismissal, or other final disposition of the \ncase or when the court finds that you are not eligible for a fee waiver.   \n• \nAPP-015/FW-015-INFO \nPage 2 of 2\nRev. April 1, 2024\nINFORMATION SHEET ON WAIVER OF APPELLATE COURT FEES— \nSUPREME COURT, COURT OF APPEAL, APPELLATE DIVISION\nPrint this form\nSave this form--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms/all-by-category)\nciteturn2146search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago;   * APP-016-GC Order on Court Fee Waiver (Court of Appeal or Supreme Court) (Ward or Conservatee) Effective: January 1, 2021 español ...   * FW-016-GC Order on Court Fee Waiver (Court of Appeal or Supreme Court) (Ward or Conservatee) Effective: January 1, 2021 español\n\n  * FW-010-GC * Notice to Court of Improved Financial Situation or Settlement (Ward or Conservatee) Effective: September 1, 2015 español\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * FW-011 * Notice to Appear for Reconsideration of Fee Waiver Effective: July 1, 2009 español\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * FW-011-GC * Notice to Appear for Reconsideration of Fee Waiver (Ward or Conservatee) Effective: September 1, 2015 español\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * FW-012 * Order on Court Fee Waiver After Reconsideration Hearing (Superior Court) Effective: September 1, 2019 español\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * FW-012-GC * Order on Court Fee Waiver After Reconsideration Hearing (Superior Court) (Ward or Conservatee) Effective: September 1, 2019 español\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * FW-015-INFO * Information Sheet on Waiver of Appellate Court Fees—Supreme Court, Court of Appeal, Appellate Division Effective: March 1, 2026 汉语 한국어 español Tiếng Việt\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * FW-016 Order on Court Fee Waiver (Court of Appeal or Supreme Court) Effective: July 1, 2010 español\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * FW-016-GC Order on Court Fee Waiver (Court of Appeal or Supreme Court) (Ward or Conservatee) Effective: January 1, 2021 español\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * FW-020 Request for Court Reporter by Party with Fee Waiver Effective: January 1, 2021\n\nSee form info Download\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nClaim of exemption for wage garnishment | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/claim-exemption-wage-garnishment)\nciteturn2146search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Financial Statement (form WG-007/EJ-165)\n\n# Make a claim of exemption for wage garnishment\n\nWage garnishment is when a debt collector has your employer take up to 20% of your wages to pay the money you owe. If, after the money is taken from your paycheck, you can’t pay for your family’s basic needs, you can file a Claim of Exemption to reduce the amount.\n\n## Important things to know\n\n  * By law, your employer cannot fire you for a single wage garnishment.\n  * The sooner you act, the sooner your wage garnishment can be stopped or reduced. \n\n## How to make a Claim of Exemption\n\n  * ### Fill out forms\n\nFill out two forms:\n\n    1. Claim of Exemption (form WG-006)\n    2. Financial Statement (form WG-007/EJ-165)\n\nOr, use a free online app to help you complete these forms.  If you use the app, you will need to print your forms once you're done.\n\nMake two copies of your completed forms. Keep one copy for yourself.  \n\n  * ### Take the forms to the Levying Officer\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPP-015/FW-015-INFO (https://courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/courts/default/2024-10/jc-20150219-itema2.pdf)\nciteturn2146search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.7 years ago; Crawled: 11.6 years ago; APP-015/FW-015-INFO\nAPP-015/FW-015-INFO\n\nINFORMATION SHEET ON WAIVER OF APPELLATE COURT FEES  \n(SUPREME COURT, COURT OF APPEAL, APPELLATE DIVISION)\n\nIf you file an appeal, a petition for a writ, or a petition for review in a civil case, such as a family law case or a case in which you sued someone or someone sued you, you must generally pay a filing fee to the court. If you are a party other than the party who filed the appeal or the petition, you must also generally pay a fee when you file your first document in a case in the Court of Appeal or Supreme Court. You and the other parties in the case may also have to pay other court fees in these proceedings, such as fees to prepare or get a copy of a clerk’s transcript in an appeal. However, if you cannot afford to pay these court fees and costs, you may ask the court to issue an order saying you do not have to pay these fees (this is called “waiving” these fees).\n\n1. Who can get their court fees waived? The court will waive your court fees and costs if:  \n• You are getting public assistance, such as Medi-Cal, Food Stamps, Supplemental Security Income (not Social Security), State Supplemental Payment, County Relief/General Assistance, In-Home Supportive Services, CalWORKS, Tribal Temporary Assistance for Needy Families, or Cash Assistance Program for Aged, Blind, and Disabled.  \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWage Garnishment | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://www.selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/wage-garnishment)\nciteturn2146search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Financial Statement (form WG-007/EJ-165)\n\n# Making a Claim of Exemption for wage garnishment\n\n  * ###### Wage garnishment is when the debt collector has your employer take up to 20% of your wages to pay the money you owe.\n\n  * ###### By law, your employer cannot fire you for a single wage garnishment.\n\n  * ###### The sooner you act, the sooner your wage garnishment can be stopped or reduced.\n\nIf after the money is taken from your paycheck, you can’t pay for your family’s basic needs, then you can file a \"Claim of Exemption.\"  A Claim of Exemption is a way to ask to lower the amount being taken.\n\n## How to make a Claim of Exemption\n\n  * ### Prepare the Claim of Exemption\n\nFill out two forms:\n\n    1. Claim of Exemption (form WG-006)\n    2. Financial Statement (form WG-007/EJ-165)\n\nOr, use a free online app to help you complete these forms.  You will need to print your forms once you're done.\n\nMake two copies of your completed forms.  Keep one copy for yourself.  \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n02-28-24-lm_0 (https://sonoma.courts.ca.gov/system/files/tentative-rulings/02-28-24-lm_0.pdf)\nciteturn2146search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.6 years ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; Neither party has filed with the court Judicial Council Form WG-007/EJ-165 (debtor’s Financial Statement).\nDefendant must demonstrate by affidavit that defendant is a “mere stakeholder with no interest in the amount or any portion thereof and that conflicting demands have been made upon him for the amount by parties to the action....” (C.C.P. § 386.5.) On noticed motion, the court may in its discretion order such relief. (Ibid.)\n\nHere, CSLB has sufficiently demonstrated that it is merely the holder of $15,000 bond deposited and otherwise has no interest or involvement otherwise in this matter. (Affidavit of Fogt, ¶¶ 3-5.) As no party has opposed this motion, the Court will grant the relief requested.\n\n## CONCLUSION\n\nBased on the foregoing, CSLB’s motion is **GRANTED**. CSLB shall submit a proposed order consistent with this tentative ruling and in accordance with California Rules of Court, Rule 3.1312.\n\n**2. 23CV00612, Coverston v. Silva**\n\n**CONTINUED** to March 20, 2024, at 3:00 pm. Neither party has filed with the court Judicial Council Form WG-007/EJ-165 (debtor’s Financial Statement). The Court has no information from which to make a decision on the claim for exemption. If the forms are not filed prior to the re-set hearing date, an order to show cause re sanctions will be issued and a hearing date for the order to show cause will be set.\n\n**3. 23CV00658, County of Sonoma v. Alvarez**\n\nPlaintiff County of Sonoma’s (the “County”) unopposed demurrer to Defendants Ignacio and Idolina Alvarez’s (together “Defendants”) amended answer to the complaint is **SUSTAINED**\n\n2--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMake a claim of exemption for wage garnishment | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/make-claim-exemption-wage-garnishment)\nciteturn2146search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;        * Financial Statement (form WG-007/EJ-165) ↗️\n\n# Make a claim of exemption for wage garnishment\n\nWage garnishment is when the debt collector has your employer take up to 20% of your wages to pay the money you owe. If this prevents you for paying for your family’s basic needs, you can file a Claim of Exemption to ask to lower the amount being taken.\n\n## Important things to know\n\n  * By law, your employer cannot fire you for a single wage garnishment.\n  * The sooner you act, the sooner your wage garnishment can be stopped or reduced.\n\n## How to make a Claim of Exemption\n\n↗️ Links to court forms below will open in a new tab.\n\n  * ### Prepare the Claim of Exemption\n\n    1. Fill out two forms:\n       * Claim of Exemption (form WG-006) ↗️\n       * Financial Statement (form WG-007/EJ-165) ↗️\n    2. Make two copies of your completed forms. \n    3. Keep one copy for yourself.  \n\n  * ### File the Claim of Exemption\n\n    1. Take or mail the original and one copy to the levying officer identified in the upper right-hand corner of the Earnings Withholding Order (form WG-002). \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRule 8.26. Waiver of fees and costs | Judicial Branch of California (https://courts.ca.gov/cms/rules/index/eight/rule8_26)\nciteturn2146search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; The clerk must provide Request to Waive Court Fees (form FW-001) or Request to Waive Court Fees (Ward or Conservatee) (form FW-001-GC) and the Information Sheet on Waiver of Fees and Costs (Supreme Court, Court of Appeal, or Appellate Division) (form APP-015/FW-015-INFO) without charge to any person who requests any fee waiver application or states that he or she is unable to pay any court fee or cost.\n"
